# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the NP9 long-answer window (tp4/np9-answer32k; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/np9-answer32k and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-np9-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-np9-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint with its own converted-weight directory (never the base's) and, since NP9, the output ceiling of its
# catalog entry (qwen_c2_checkpoints.json "request": output_budget 32768, default_max_tokens 16384). A job without them is the base: its ceiling is the profile's 16,384, so the long-answer tests would read as clamped.
# N1 (STOP): ONE request at a time, 30,000 tokens, on Swift. warmup; concurrent8_steady (the profile's required eight-user check, which also proves the octo rounds still
# run); long_answer_prefix (one 4k real-code prompt asked at max_tokens 16,384 and then 30,000, both ignore_eos: the long answer must begin with the short one but for its
# last 512 characters - greedy decoding does not change with the ceiling, the budget enters a round only at the last few tokens); long_answer_solo_4k (a 4k prompt, 30,000
# tokens, ignore_eos) and long_answer_solo_200k (a 200,000-token prompt as the server counts it, 30,000 tokens, ignore_eos: the answer ends at position 230,000 and the
# request reserves 3,596 of the pool's 16,499 blocks). CEILING READ: the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] request output budget 32768 for this checkpoint (its catalog entry;
# the profile says 16384)" and "[QWEN-C2] request contract installed: greedy, max_tokens <= 32768" (c2_smoke_check requires the second whenever a long-answer test ran), the
# checkpoint lines (c2_smoke_check --expect-checkpoint) and no "kv reservation too large" line. ANSWER READ (c2_smoke_check, long_answer_problems): every user of a
# long_answer test ends with finish "length" and exactly 30,000 tokens (ignore_eos, so the stop is the ceiling, not the model); fewer tokens at "length" is a server whose
# ceiling clamped the request. MEMORY READ: the output ceiling allocates no verifier capture, proposal bucket or page table (docs/tp4-np9-answer32k.md), so the DRAM lines
# are the ship-4 profile's own: no "dram backstop refused", no "dram admission hold" that the same prompts would not have drawn at 16,384, no engine-build failure, no
# "audit mismatch", no stall. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED (a model load under CI load has hit the platform's load timeout; the decodes here run 7 to 30 minutes). READ also: the
# solo decode rate is recorded, never gated; the stream never stalls for the answer's 7 to 15 minutes (a gap over the profile's QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_MAX_DECODE_GAP_S, 8 s, is a
# fault). Stop rule: a request that ends short of 30,000 tokens, a prefix difference, a stall, any audit mismatch or a refusal line. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1,
# scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A
# 30,000-token decode is minutes at the board power limit: a rate that falls while AICLK falls is the clock, not the ceiling. Duration (estimate): 75 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-np9-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,long_answer_prefix,long_answer_solo_4k,long_answer_solo_200k
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=150
